### 1. Get all bookings (should return empty array initially)
GET http://localhost:8081/api/bookings

### 2. Create a valid booking (return 201)
POST http://localhost:8081/api/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "eventId": "EV001",
  "participantName": "Rahim Gonzalez",
  "participantEmail": "rahim@example.com",
  "seats": 2
}

### 3. Get the created booking (return 200)
GET http://localhost:8081/api/bookings/BK001

### 4. Create a booking with missing fields (return 400)
POST http://localhost:8081/api/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "eventId": "",
  "participantName": "",
  "participantEmail": "",
  "seats": 0
}

### 5. Create a booking with invalid event ID (return 404)
POST http://localhost:8081/api/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "eventId": "EV999",
  "participantName": "Rahim Gonzalez",
  "participantEmail": "rahim@example.com",
  "seats": 2
}

### 6. Create a booking with too many seats (return 400)
POST http://localhost:8081/api/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "eventId": "EV002",
  "participantName": "Rahim Gonzalez",
  "participantEmail": "rahim@example.com",
  "seats": 100
}

### 7. Delete a booking (return 200)
DELETE http://localhost:8081/api/bookings/BK001

### 8. Get the cancelled booking (return status CANCELLED)
GET http://localhost:8081/api/bookings/BK001

### 9. Verify seat restoration on event EV001 (reflect restored seats)
GET http://localhost:8081/api/events
